          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: сессия",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "сессия (séssiya) — \"an exam period (at university); a session\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "В январе у студентов сессия. V yanvaré u studéntov séssiya. In January the students have their exams."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine. At a Russian university, the weeks of exams at the end of each term. Сдавать сессию — to sit one’s exams."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "сессия (séssiya) is usually traced, through western languages, to Latin sessiō \"a sitting\" (Lewis & Short), built on sedēre \"to sit\": a time when a body sits to do its business."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
